{"chunk_id": "45bf23cd23fe", "text": "Narada recounts the devastation caused by the Asura brothers Sunda and Upasunda. Having gained immense power, they roam the world in shifting forms\u2014elephants, lions, and tigers\u2014hunting down sages and destroying sacred life. Sacrifices cease, trade stops, agriculture is abandoned, and the earth becomes a desolate field of bones. The gods, sages, and celestial beings, distressed by the collapse of cosmic order, appeal to Brahma for a solution. Brahma devises a subtle strategy: he orders the divine craftsman Viswakarman to create a woman of incomparable beauty. From the finest features of all creation emerges Tilottama, a celestial maiden whose beauty captivates even the gods. Her task is to enchant the inseparable brothers so that rivalry and desire will cause them to destroy each other, restoring balance to the world.\nThe gods appeal to Brahma about the destructive Asura brothers, and he creates the irresistible maiden Tilottama to provoke them into conflict.\nThemes: divine intervention, cosmic disorder, beauty as strategy, creation of Tilottama, rivalry of Sunda and Upasunda", "vector": [-0.011371991597115993, -0.021732840687036514, -0.006258977111428976, -0.006218531634658575, 0.005969115998595953, 0.013684139586985111, -0.042306236922740936, -0.001145962392911315, -0.0037446008063852787, -0.021072227507829666, 0.00029828728293068707, 0.004438919015228748, 0.012652773410081863, 0.0010583300609141588, 0.0004878766485489905, 0.013677398674190044, 0.04058055207133293, -0.005139978602528572, 0.011722521856427193, -0.0203846488147974, -0.005187165457755327, -0.0010608579032123089, 0.007772321812808514, 0.026370618492364883, -0.024860644713044167, 0.004806301090866327, 0.03208694979548454, -0.037965063005685806, -0.009700234979391098, -0.003250825684517622, -0.010037282481789589, -0.0054568033665418625, -0.015018848702311516, -0.004728780128061771, -0.018443254753947258, -0.001365043455734849, -0.00016578537179157138, -0.